Rem Turtle demo: a colour-cycling spiral. Run with
Rem     mill run tst/turtle-demo.shoddy
Rem This is the "open, draw, return" shape — there is no event loop. Main
Rem returns once the drawing is blitted; the window stays up until the
Rem user closes it. The whole picture is one Fold over Range: each step
Rem recolours (the RGB channels wrap with the Wrap builtin), steps
Rem forward a little further, and turns 91 degrees so the square spiral
Rem slowly precesses. LOGO's REPEAT is Shoddy's Fold.

Include "../machines/turtle.shoddy"
Rem Stamp() is clock's, and must be included in its own right: turtle's
Rem own includes are linked, not re-exported, once it is a machine DLL.
Include "../machines/clock.shoddy"

Def Spin(t As Turtle, i As Number) As Turtle
    Let hue = SetPenColor(t, Wrap(i * 9, 256), Wrap(i * 5 + 90, 256), Wrap(300 - i * 4, 256))
    TurnRight(Forward(hue, i * 2), 91)

Def Main()
    Let t = Title(NewTurtle(640, 480), "Shoddy Turtle - spiral")
    Let done = Fold(Range(1, 160), t, Fn(t, i) => Spin(t, i))
    Let shown = Blit(done)
    Print("turtle done " & Stamp())
